WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.588
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 1, Networking concepts, which is 23 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.588 --> 00:00:10.153
This lesson covers objective 1 point 8.

00:00:10.153 --> 00:00:14.163
Summarize evolving use cases for modern network environments.

00:00:14.163 --> 00:00:19.620
Today's concept: why a branch user's email goes straight to the cloud in an SD-WAN.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.690
A branch office, a headquarters, and a cloud email service.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:30.194
The old way sent everything to headquarters first, and then out to the cloud.

00:00:30.194 --> 00:00:33.060
That detour is called hairpinning, and it adds delay.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:42.860
With SD-WAN local breakout, the branch edge device recognizes the application and sends trusted cloud traffic straight to the nearest service.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.632
DHCP is not the reason.

00:00:44.632 --> 00:00:47.806
It only gives out an address and a default gateway.

00:00:47.806 --> 00:00:50.420
It does not choose a path per application.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:01:00.728
For the exam, when branch cloud traffic skips headquarters, the answer is local breakout, driven by application-aware policy.

00:01:00.728 --> 00:01:03.529
DHCP only hands out addresses and a gateway.

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:05.630
That's objective one point eight.
